IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part III, "Employment Insurance Operating Account": sections 70.2 to 80.1.
-- What is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund, what is credited to and charged against the Employment Insurance
-- Operating Account, how benefits are paid (special warrants), the yearly forecasts, the cap on Part II spending, and
-- interest on amounts owing to Her Majesty.
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- These are provisions about the Crown's accounts. Where a section sorts a kind of money (ss 72, 75, 77) the kind is a
-- constructor of `ei3 Kind of amount` or `ei3 Kind of payment`, and the rule answers JUST TRUE for a kind the section
-- names and NOTHING (not covered) for a kind it does not: a section that lists what is paid in says nothing about what is
-- not listed, and the encoding never answers FALSE for it.
-- Section 80.1(1) (the power to make regulations) is machinery and is not encoded; see NOTES.md.

§ `Section 70.2 - the Account`

DECLARE `ei3 Account in the accounts of Canada` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 the Employment Insurance Operating Account`

-- src:1229 | 70.2 There is established in the accounts of Canada an account to be known as the Employment Insurance Operating Account.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 70.2 (src:1229)
GIVETH A `ei3 Account in the accounts of Canada`
`s 70.2 the account established in the accounts of Canada` MEANS `ei3 the Employment Insurance Operating Account`

§ `Sections 72 and 75 - kinds of money paid in and credited`

-- The kinds of amount sections 72 and 75 sort. They are mutually exclusive; the last one is the explicit "not listed".
DECLARE `ei3 Kind of amount` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 a premium`
    `ei3 a fine`
    `ei3 a penalty imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1`
    `ei3 a penalty on benefit repayment`
    `ei3 a penalty of another kind`
    `ei3 interest under section 80.1`
    `ei3 interest on benefit repayment`
    `ei3 interest of another kind`
    `ei3 repayment of overpaid benefits`
    `ei3 benefit repayment`
    `ei3 an amount collected for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public`
    `ei3 principal or interest on a loan made by the Commission under Part II`
    `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under section 61 for employment support measures`
    `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under an agreement entered into under section 63`
    `ei3 repayment of another overpayment made by the Commission under Part II`
    `ei3 an amount of a kind these sections do not list`

-- Section 72: (a) is limited to amounts "received under Parts I and III to IX"; (b) is not; (c) is the Part II money.
-- If paragraph (a)'s kind was not received under those Parts, the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1232 | 72 There shall be paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund
-- src:1233 | (a) all amounts received under Parts I and III to IX, as or on account of premiums, fines, penalties, interest, repayment of overpaid benefits and benefit repayment;
-- src:1234 | (b) all amounts collected by the Commission for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public; and
-- src:1235 | (c) all amounts received on account of principal or interest on loans made by the Commission under Part II or as repayment of overpayments made by the Commission under that Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 72 (src:1232-1235)
GIVEN kind IS A `ei3 Kind of amount`
      `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ei3 a premium` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 a fine` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 a penalty imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 a penalty on benefit repayment` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 a penalty of another kind` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 interest under section 80.1` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 interest on benefit repayment` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 interest of another kind` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 repayment of overpaid benefits` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 benefit repayment` THEN IF `it was received under Parts I and III to IX` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `ei3 an amount collected for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 principal or interest on a loan made by the Commission under Part II` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under section 61 for employment support measures` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under an agreement entered into under section 63` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 repayment of another overpayment made by the Commission under Part II` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 an amount of a kind these sections do not list` THEN NOTHING

-- Section 75: "all amounts paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund that are" (a) penalties imposed under section 38, 39
-- or 65.1 and repayments of overpaid benefits, "except interest and penalties on benefit repayment"; (b) services;
-- (c) loans under Part II; (d) section 61 overpayments; (e) section 63 agreement overpayments; (f) interest under 80.1.
-- Premiums, fines and the rest are credited by other sections (s 73(a) for premiums), not by this one: NOTHING.
-- src:1246 | 75 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account all amounts paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund that are
-- src:1247 | (a) received as or on account of penalties imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1 and repayments of overpaid benefits, except interest and penalties on benefit repayment;
-- src:1248 | (b) collected by the Commission for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public;
-- src:1249 | (c) received on account of principal or interest on loans made by the Commission under Part II;
-- src:1250 | (d) received as repayments of overpayments by the Commission under section 61 for employment support measures authorized by Part II;
-- src:1251 | (e) received as repayments of overpayments by the Commission under agreements entered into under section 63; or
-- src:1252 | (f) received as interest under section 80.1.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 75 (src:1246-1252)
GIVEN kind IS A `ei3 Kind of amount`
      `it was paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` IS
    IF (NOT `it was paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `ei3 a penalty imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `ei3 repayment of overpaid benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `ei3 an amount collected for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `ei3 principal or interest on a loan made by the Commission under Part II` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under section 61 for employment support measures` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under an agreement entered into under section 63` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `ei3 interest under section 80.1` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Sections 73 to 74 - credits to the Account`

-- Section 73: three credits, charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund; the credit for a year is their sum.
-- src:1237 | 73 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund
-- src:1238 | (a) an amount in each year equal to the amount receivable as or on account of premiums payable for that year under this Act;
-- src:1239 | (b) any other amounts provided out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund appropriated by Parliament for any purpose related to employment insurance and administered by the Commission; and
-- src:1240 | (c) an amount equal to all benefit repayments receivable under Part VII.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 73 (src:1237-1240)
GIVEN `the amount receivable as or on account of premiums payable for that year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `any other amounts provided out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund appropriated by Parliament for any purpose related to employment insurance and administered by the Commission` IS A NUMBER
      `all benefit repayments receivable under Part VII` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 73 the amount credited to the Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund for the year` IS
    `the amount receivable as or on account of premiums payable for that year under this Act`
        PLUS `any other amounts provided out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund appropriated by Parliament for any purpose related to employment insurance and administered by the Commission`
        PLUS `all benefit repayments receivable under Part VII`

-- Section 73.1: credited ON August 1, 2010; "the cost is estimated to be $2,900,000,000" is the estimate in the budget of
-- January 27, 2009, not the amount credited, which is whatever the Minister of Finance determines corresponds to the cost.
-- src:1242 | 73.1 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account on August 1, 2010 the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the cost of the benefit enhancement measures under this Act, provided for in the budget tabled in Parliament on January 27, 2009 in which the cost is estimated to be $2,900,000,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 73.1 (src:1242)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 73.1 the day on which the amount is credited` MEANS YearMonthDay 2010 8 1

-- src:1242 | 73.1 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account on August 1, 2010 the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the cost of the benefit enhancement measures under this Act, provided for in the budget tabled in Parliament on January 27, 2009 in which the cost is estimated to be $2,900,000,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 73.1 (src:1242)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 73.1 the day on which the budget was tabled in Parliament` MEANS YearMonthDay 2009 1 27

-- src:1242 | 73.1 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account on August 1, 2010 the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the cost of the benefit enhancement measures under this Act, provided for in the budget tabled in Parliament on January 27, 2009 in which the cost is estimated to be $2,900,000,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 73.1 (src:1242)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 73.1 the cost of the benefit enhancement measures estimated in the budget` MEANS 2_900_000_000

-- src:1242 | 73.1 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account on August 1, 2010 the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the cost of the benefit enhancement measures under this Act, provided for in the budget tabled in Parliament on January 27, 2009 in which the cost is estimated to be $2,900,000,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 73.1 (src:1242)
GIVEN `the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the cost of the benefit enhancement measures` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 73.1 the amount credited to the Account on August 1, 2010` IS
    `the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the cost of the benefit enhancement measures`

-- Section 74: the Crown as employer: the credit equals the employer's premiums Her Majesty in right of Canada must pay.
-- src:1244 | 74 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund an amount equal to the premiums required to be paid by Her Majesty in right of Canada as employer’s premiums for persons employed in insurable employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 74 (src:1244)
GIVEN `the premiums required to be paid by Her Majesty in right of Canada as employer's premiums for persons employed in insurable employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 74 the amount credited to the Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS
    `the premiums required to be paid by Her Majesty in right of Canada as employer's premiums for persons employed in insurable employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada`

§ `Sections 77 to 79 - charges to the Account, special warrants, forecasts, the cap and the plan`

DECLARE `ei3 Kind of payment out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 amounts paid as or on account of benefits under this Act`
    `ei3 amounts paid under section 61 for employment support measures`
    `ei3 amounts paid under paragraph 63(1)(a)`
    `ei3 the costs of administering this Act, including administration fees or costs paid under section 62 or paragraph 63(1)(b)`
    `ei3 the costs of administering sections 28.1 and 28.2 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`
    `ei3 the costs of administering Part 5 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of appeals respecting this Act`
    `ei3 a payment of a kind section 77(1) does not list`

-- Section 77(1): paragraphs (e) and (f) are repealed. A payment of a listed kind is charged to the Account; for any other
-- kind the subsection says nothing.
-- src:1255 | 77 (1) There shall be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Employment Insurance Operating Account
-- src:1256 | (a) all amounts paid as or on account of benefits under this Act;
-- src:1257 | (b) all amounts paid under section 61 for employment support measures;
-- src:1258 | (c) all amounts paid under paragraph 63(1)(a);
-- src:1259 | (d) the costs of administering this Act, including administration fees or costs paid under section 62 or paragraph 63(1)(b);
-- src:1260 | (d.1) the costs of administering sections 28.1 and 28.2 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act; and
-- src:1261 | (e) and (f) [Repealed, 2012, c. 31, s. 439]
-- src:1262 | (g) the costs of administering Part 5 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of appeals respecting this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 77(1) (src:1255-1262)
GIVEN kind IS A `ei3 Kind of payment out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ei3 a payment of a kind section 77(1) does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 77(2): benefits "shall be paid by special warrants"; section 61 and 63(1)(a) amounts "may be".
DECLARE `ei3 How an amount is to be paid by special warrant` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 shall be paid by special warrants`
    `ei3 may be paid by special warrants`

-- src:1264 | (2) Notwithstanding the Financial Administration Act, amounts mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) shall be paid by special warrants drawn on the Receiver General and issued by the Commission by electronic means or bearing the printed signature of the Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson of the Commission, and amounts mentioned in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) may be paid by the special warrants.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 77(2) (src:1264)
GIVEN kind IS A `ei3 Kind of payment out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei3 How an amount is to be paid by special warrant`
DECIDE `s 77(2) the way the amount is paid by special warrant` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ei3 amounts paid as or on account of benefits under this Act` THEN JUST `ei3 shall be paid by special warrants`
    WHEN `ei3 amounts paid under section 61 for employment support measures` THEN JUST `ei3 may be paid by special warrants`
    WHEN `ei3 amounts paid under paragraph 63(1)(a)` THEN JUST `ei3 may be paid by special warrants`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Issued "by electronic means or bearing the printed signature of the Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson of the Commission".
-- src:1264 | (2) Notwithstanding the Financial Administration Act, amounts mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) shall be paid by special warrants drawn on the Receiver General and issued by the Commission by electronic means or bearing the printed signature of the Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson of the Commission, and amounts mentioned in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) may be paid by the special warrants.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 77(2) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the special warrant is drawn on the Receiver General and issued by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is issued by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it bears the printed signature of the Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 77(2) the special warrant is validly issued` IF
        `the special warrant is drawn on the Receiver General and issued by the Commission`
    AND (`it is issued by electronic means` OR `it bears the printed signature of the Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson of the Commission`)

-- Section 77(3): "negotiable without charge at any financial institution in Canada": the holder pays nothing to cash it.
-- src:1266 | (3) The special warrants are negotiable without charge at any financial institution in Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 77(3) (src:1266)
GIVEN `the document is a special warrant under subsection 77(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a financial institution in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 77(3) the special warrant is negotiable without charge at the institution` IS
    IF `the document is a special warrant under subsection 77(2)` AND `the institution is a financial institution in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 77.1: "On or before July 22 in a year": the Minister of Finance's two steps (a) and the Minister's step (b).
-- src:1268 | 77.1 On or before July 22 in a year,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 77.1 (src:1268)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 77.1 the day on or before which the forecasts and estimates are to be made` IS
    YearMonthDay year 7 22

-- src:1268 | 77.1 On or before July 22 in a year,
-- src:1269 | (a) the Minister of Finance shall
-- src:1270 | (i) forecast the amount to be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account under sections 73 to 75 during the year,
-- src:1271 | (ii) forecast the amount to be charged, during the year, to that Account under subsection 77(1) based on, among other things, information provided by the Minister, and
-- src:1272 | (iii) estimate the total, at December 31 of the immediately preceding year, of the amounts credited to that Account; and
-- src:1273 | (b) the Minister shall estimate the total, at December 31 of the immediately preceding year, of the amounts charged to that Account.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 77.1 (src:1268-1273)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Minister of Finance made the forecasts and the estimate under paragraph (a)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Minister made the estimate under paragraph (b)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 77.1 the forecasts and estimates were made in time` IF
        `the day on which the Minister of Finance made the forecasts and the estimate under paragraph (a)` AT MOST `s 77.1 the day on or before which the forecasts and estimates are to be made` year
    AND `the day on which the Minister made the estimate under paragraph (b)` AT MOST `s 77.1 the day on or before which the forecasts and estimates are to be made` year

-- Section 78: 0.8% of the insurable earnings "from which the prescribed amount is deducted ... as employee's premiums, as
-- estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates"; the total paid out "must not exceed" it.
-- src:1276 | 78 The total amount that may be paid out by the Commission under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) and charged to the Employment Insurance Operating Account under this Part in a fiscal year must not exceed 0.8% of the insurable earnings of all insured persons from which the prescribed amount is deducted under subsection 82(1) in that year as or on account of employee’s premiums, as estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 78 (src:1276)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings of all insured persons from which the prescribed amount is deducted in the fiscal year, as estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 78 the most that may be paid out under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) in the fiscal year` IS
    (0.8%) TIMES `the insurable earnings of all insured persons from which the prescribed amount is deducted in the fiscal year, as estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates`

-- src:1276 | 78 The total amount that may be paid out by the Commission under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) and charged to the Employment Insurance Operating Account under this Part in a fiscal year must not exceed 0.8% of the insurable earnings of all insured persons from which the prescribed amount is deducted under subsection 82(1) in that year as or on account of employee’s premiums, as estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 78 (src:1276)
GIVEN `the total paid out by the Commission under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) and charged to the Account in the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the insurable earnings of all insured persons from which the prescribed amount is deducted in the fiscal year, as estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 78 the total paid out is within the maximum` IF
    `the total paid out by the Commission under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) and charged to the Account in the fiscal year`
        AT MOST `s 78 the most that may be paid out under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) in the fiscal year` `the insurable earnings of all insured persons from which the prescribed amount is deducted in the fiscal year, as estimated by the Commission and set out in the Main Estimates`

-- src:1278 | 79 The Minister shall, with the concurrence of the Minister of Finance,
-- src:1279 | (a) submit to the Treasury Board for approval a plan for each fiscal year estimating the amounts to be paid for that year under Part II; and
-- src:1280 | (b) have the plan included in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for the fiscal year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 79 (src:1278-1280)
GIVEN `the Minister, with the concurrence of the Minister of Finance, submitted to the Treasury Board for approval a plan for the fiscal year estimating the amounts to be paid under Part II` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister had the plan included in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for the fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 79 the Minister has done what the section requires` IF
        `the Minister, with the concurrence of the Minister of Finance, submitted to the Treasury Board for approval a plan for the fiscal year estimating the amounts to be paid under Part II`
    AND `the Minister had the plan included in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for the fiscal year`

§ `Section 80.1 - interest on amounts owing to Her Majesty`

-- Subsection (2): interest payable under section 80.1 is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable in the Federal Court, any
-- other court of competent jurisdiction, or any other manner the Act provides (including s 47(2) and s 126, in pieces ei2
-- and ei4).
-- src:1288 | (2) Interest payable under this section is a debt due to Her Majesty and may be recovered in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act, including the manner in which an amount owing under Part I may be recovered under subsection 47(2) or section 126.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 80.1(2) (src:1288)
GIVEN `the interest is payable under section 80.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 80.1(2) the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty` IF
    `the interest is payable under section 80.1`

-- Subsection (3): "No interest ... may be recovered more than 72 months after the day on which the liability to pay it
-- arose": recovery on the day exactly 72 months after is not "more than" 72 months after, so it is still allowed.
-- `add months` clamps to the last day of a shorter month (keel fork F4).
-- src:1290 | (3) No interest due under this section may be recovered more than 72 months after the day on which the liability to pay it arose.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 80.1(3) (src:1290)
GIVEN `the day on which the liability to pay the interest arose` IS A DATE
      `the day on which recovery of the interest is sought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 80.1(3) the interest may still be recovered` IF
    `the day on which recovery of the interest is sought` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which the liability to pay the interest arose` 72)

-- Subsection (4): section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act does not apply to amounts owing "other than Parts IV
-- and VII". For an amount owing under Part IV or VII the subsection is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:1292 | (4) Section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act does not apply in relation to amounts owing to Her Majesty under this Act, other than Parts IV and VII.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 80.1(4) (src:1292)
GIVEN `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under Part IV or Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 80.1(4) section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies` IS
    IF `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under Part IV or Part VII`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE
